  "goodToKnow": "Die Basilika is a basilica, originally a Roman hall and later a church with a high central nave, or an honorary title granted by the Pope. Trier's Konstantinbasilika, Emperor Constantine's throne hall from around 310 AD, is the largest surviving Roman single-room building and now a Protestant church. Stressed on the second syllable. Don't confuse it with das Basilikum (basil). Plural: die Basiliken."
